Body:
I can still reproduce this on OpenCode 1.18.18 with google/gemini-3.7-flash.
The MCP tool exposes this schema, generated by github.com/google/jsonschema-go v0.4.2:
```
{
  "type": ["null", "array"],
  "items": {
    "type": "integer"
  }
}
```
OpenCode appears to project it to roughly:
```
{
  "nullable": true,
  "items": {
    "type": "integer"
  },
  "anyOf": [
    {
      "type": "array"
    }
  ]
}
```
Gemini then returns:
```
parameters.properties[device_ids].items: field predicate failed: $type == Type.ARRAY
parameters.properties[device_ids].any_of[0].items: missing field.
```
It looks like items remains on the outer schema while the array type moves into anyOf. Nullable objects have the same problem with properties and required.
Disabling the MCP server makes the request succeed. Changing the MCP schema to use "type": "array" also fixes it.
This may be a remaining case in the nullable type-array handling added by #41109. For a union containing null and one other type, could the projection keep the non-null type and its constraints together, then add nullable: true?

FYI this works in the config so the top p 1.0 gets overridden with what you have in the model config (in opencode's json file)

"Qwen3.8-27B": {
    "name": "Qwen3.8-27B",
    "reasoning": true,
    "tool_call": true,
    "options": {
        "top_p": 0.95
    },
    "limit": {
        "context": 260000,
        "output": 128535
    }
},
